~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] How to read the summary
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Each experiment (including the leaky diagnostics Bleaky / Cleaky) is compared with R2 values
  reported in the         original paper (PAPER_R2). 'NOT significantly different'         means
  the published value lies inside our 95% CI, i.e. we reproduce it within sampling uncertainty.
  p_boot is the         fraction of bootstrap resamples that fall on the other side of the
  reference value (small = real difference).
  The paired delta R2 lines then ask whether adding feature selection (B vs A) or augmentation (C
  vs B / C vs A) truly         improved the model. If the CI of a delta includes 0, the
  improvement cannot be distinguished from noise.         The leaky deltas (Bleaky vs A / B,
  Cleaky vs C) show how much selecting bits on the test set inflates the score.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
