REDOCKING VALIDATION PIPELINE — Crystal Ligand Re-Docking
Timestamp: 2026-10-23 10:35:12
Receptor setup: Chain B (DHFR active site) of PDB 6AOG
================================================================================
Target Criterion: heavy-atom RMSD < 2.0 Å = Protocol Validated


~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Before trusting docking scores for new drugs, we check that the docking software can reproduce a
  known answer. The         crystal structure 6AOG contains the real inhibitor pyrimethamine (CP6)
  bound to the TgDHFR active site. We         take that ligand out, place it back with AutoDock
  Vina (a physics-based scoring program that searches positions and         orientations of a
  molecule inside a search box), and compare where Vina puts it with where it sits in the crystal.
  Pass criterion: the heavy-atom RMSD between the docked pose and the crystal ligand must be below
  2.0 Å         (1 Å = 0.1 nm, about one bond length), which also checks the orientation of the
  ligand. The distance between the two         geometric centres is reported as well, but note
  that the search box is centred on the crystal ligand.
  The same search box (centre and size in paths_config.py) is then reused for all FDA drugs in
  step 07.         Binding affinity is in kcal/mol: more negative = predicted tighter binding.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
